+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Standing state
+
+- `RIGGING.md` is not fitted yet. Greenfield bootstrap: production code and rigging are absent. Shipwright fits out `RIGGING.md` and `AGENTS.md` (specs dir `features/`, runner `cucumber-js`, DOM `happy-dom`, `prove`/`verify`/`sweep`/`plank-join` methods, and tiers) before any tier-tagged QM watch runs. The current `watchbill.json` references scenarios by path only, no tier tags, so it runs under the default tier once rigging exists.
+- The `features/` specs-directory convention and the `cucumber-js` + `happy-dom` runner are fixed by `README.md`. Step definitions belong under `features/support/` (QM's job).
+
+## Decisions captured in durable specs
+
+- Persistence key name is `todos-vanilla` (the TodoMVC `todos-[framework]` convention for the vanilla example). Pinned by `features/persistence.feature:Todos are stored under the todos-vanilla key with id, title and completed`.
+- Routing is hash-based (`#/`, `#/active`, `#/completed`). The spec names the Flatiron Director library for non-framework apps, but no Director bundle is present in the tree, so the implementation is expected to use a vanilla `hashchange` listener. Crew decides at implementation; behaviour is pinned by `features/routing.feature`.
+
+## Open questions
+
+- None blocking. Awaiting Shipwright fit-out of `RIGGING.md` before outbound or harbour.
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0a7f4a5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+Feature: Todo persistence
+  As a user of the TodoMVC app
+  I want my todos to persist across reloads
+  So that I do not lose my list
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist to localStorage across reload
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+      | Second | true      |
+    When the user reloads the page
+    Then the todo list contains "First"
+    And the todo list contains "Second"
+    And the todo "Second" has class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Todos are stored under the todos-vanilla key with id, title and completed
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+    Then localStorage item "todos-vanilla" is a JSON array
+    And each stored todo has the keys "id", "title" and "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Editing state is not persisted across reload
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+    When the user begins editing the todo "First"
+    And the user reloads the page
+    Then the todo "First" does not have class "editing"
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..10f574c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+Feature: Todo routing and filtering
+  As a user of the TodoMVC app
+  I want to filter todos by route
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos and selects the All filter
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+      | Second | true      |
+    Then the "All" filter link has class "selected"
+    And the todo list contains "First"
+    And the todo list contains "Second"
+
+  Scenario: Active route shows only incomplete todos
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+      | Second | true      |
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
+    And the todo list contains "First"
+    And the todo list does not contain "Second"
+
+  Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+      | Second | true      |
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the "Completed" filter link has class "selected"
+    And the todo list contains "Second"
+    And the todo list does not contain "First"
+
+  Scenario: Checking a todo in the Active filter hides it
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+      | Second | true      |
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    And the user toggles the todo "First"
+    Then the todo list does not contain "First"
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists across reload
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+      | Second | true      |
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    And the user reloads the page
+    Then the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
+    And the todo list contains "First"
diff --git a/features/todos.feature b/features/todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..76c5daa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,97 @@
+Feature: Todo list core behaviour
+  As a user of the TodoMVC app
+  I want to manage my todos in the DOM
+  So that I can track what needs to be done
+
+  Scenario: Empty list hides the main and footer sections
+    Given the app loads with no todos
+    Then the "main" section is hidden
+    And the "footer" section is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Creating a todo adds it and clears the input
+    Given the app loads with no todos
+    When the user creates a todo with title "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And the new-todo input is empty
+    And the "main" section is visible
+
+  Scenario: Creating a todo trims whitespace and ignores empty input
+    Given the app loads with no todos
+    When the user creates a todo with title "   "
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo marks it completed
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+    When the user toggles the todo "First"
+    Then the todo "First" has class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Toggling all completes every todo
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+      | Second | false     |
+    When the user toggles all todos
+    Then every todo has class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all reflects when all todos are complete
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | true      |
+      | Second | true      |
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows the active todo count pluralized
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+      | Second | false     |
+      | Third  | true      |
+    Then the todo-count shows "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes completed todos
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+      | Second | true      |
+    When the user clears completed todos
+    Then the todo list contains only "First"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed is hidden when no completed todos exist
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+    Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Beginning to edit a todo enters editing mode
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+    When the user begins editing the todo "First"
+    Then the todo "First" has class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Editing saves the trimmed new title
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+    When the user begins editing the todo "First"
+    And the user renames the todo "First" to "First edited"
+    Then the todo list contains "First edited"
+
+  Scenario: Editing to empty destroys the todo
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+    When the user begins editing the todo "First"
+    And the user renames the todo "First" to "   "
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Escape cancels editing and discards changes
+    Given the app loads with todos:
+      | title  | completed |
+      | First  | false     |
+    When the user begins editing the todo "First"
+    And the user cancels editing of the todo "First"
+    Then the todo list contains "First"
+    And the todo "First" does not have class "editing"
